# Virtualenv
#
# ONLY the directory names that unambiguously mean "a virtualenv". The entries
# below used to also list bin/, lib/, lib64/, include/, Scripts/ and
# pyvenv.cfg - the contents of a venv rather than the venv itself. Every one of
# those is unanchored, so it matched at ANY depth, and git sets
# core.ignorecase=true on Windows, which made `Scripts/` match `scripts/` too.
#
# The result was silent: EzGrind/Database/scripts/ and EzGrind/Backend/scripts/
# were excluded from every commit, so a clean clone had no exercise importer, no
# EXPLAIN harness and no data-migration script, and nothing ever said so.
#
# Anything that needs ignoring inside a venv is already inside venv/.
venv/
.venv/

# An orphaned venv bin/ left at Backend level by an old `python -m venv .`.
# Named explicitly rather than with a bare `bin/`, which would match any
# directory called bin anywhere in the tree.
EzGrind/Backend/bin/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Secrets
.env

# OS
.DS_Store

# Logs
*.log

# Generated email preview (regenerate with a script, never commit)
preview_welcome_email.html

# Database backups
EzGrind/Database/backup_*.sql